                "impact": {
                  "S": "Studying the fundamentals of Bioinformatics had a significant impact on my understanding of modern biological and medical sciences because since I am a forensic scientist so it helps me combines biology, computer science, mathematics, and statistics information to analyze and interpret biological data. This field plays an important role in my research, healthcare, and biotechnology.\nIt also helps me understand complex biological information such as DNA, RNA, and protein sequences in depth. It also allows me to the analysis of large datasets generated through genomic and molecular studies.\nThe study of bioinformatics enables me to identify genes, study protein structures, and understand gene expression and mutations, which are essential in genetics and molecular biology as well as forensic investigations."
